            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 1: FAMILY LIFE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from sharing household chores and strengthening family bonds. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen household chores. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for family members to teach children responsibility and teamwork.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 1: Family Life. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to divide housework fairly at home before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and reduce stress on working mothers and strengthen family bonds in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 1: Family Life)</i>"
