            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 2: HUMANS AND THE ENVIRONMENT</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from adopting a green lifestyle and reducing our carbon footprint. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen green habits. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for citizens and students to cut down on single-use plastic waste and save energy.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 2: Humans and the Environment. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to adopt an eco-friendly lifestyle in our community before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and reduce our household carbon footprint and protect local ecosystems in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 2: Humans and the Environment)</i>"
