            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 3: MUSIC</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from enjoying traditional and modern music shows. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen musical performances. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for young musicians and audiences to connect people from different cultures and relieve daily stress.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 3: Music. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to appreciate both folk music and modern pop on the concert stage before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and inspire teenagers to learn traditional musical instruments in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 3: Music)</i>"
