            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 4: FOR A BETTER COMMUNITY</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from volunteering and helping disadvantaged people in the community. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen volunteer activities. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for student volunteers to support disadvantaged children and elderly neighbours.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 4: For a Better Community. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to take part in community service in remote communities before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and build confidence, empathy and practical life skills for teenagers in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 4: For a Better Community)</i>"
