            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 6: GENDER EQUALITY</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from promoting gender equality in education and careers. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen career opportunities. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for men and women to allow both men and women to pursue their dream careers.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 6: Gender Equality. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to promote equal rights and fair pay in the workplace before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and reduce poverty and boost economic growth for the whole society in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 6: Gender Equality)</i>"
