            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 7: VIET NAM AND INTERNATIONAL ORGANISATIONS</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from Viet Nam's active participation in international organisations. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen international programmes. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for member countries and youth delegates to improve healthcare and education for disadvantaged children.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 7: Viet Nam and International Organisations. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to cooperate closely with international organisations across Southeast Asia before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and promote trade, peacekeeping and cultural exchange worldwide in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 7: Viet Nam and International Organisations)</i>"
