            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 8: NEW WAYS TO LEARN</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about blended learning, online courses and digital tools in education. Rather than treating Unit 8: New Ways to Learn as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to combine face-to-face discussions with flexible online study.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to combine traditional and digital learning in modern classrooms. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on learning methods. Through these authentic tasks, teachers and students discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped help students develop self-study, teamwork and digital research skills. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making blended learning, online courses and digital tools in education an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 8: New Ways to Learn)</i>"
