            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 9: PROTECTING THE ENVIRONMENT</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from protecting biodiversity and stopping deforestation and wildlife trade. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen environmental programmes. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for rangers and students to prevent deforestation and protect endangered animals from poaching.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 9: Protecting the Environment. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to protect natural habitats and biodiversity in national parks before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and maintain the natural balance of ecosystems and reduce air pollution in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 9: Protecting the Environment)</i>"
