            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 10: ECOTOURISM</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from sustainable ecotourism, respecting local culture and protecting nature. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen ecotourism tours. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for eco-tourists and local guides to educate travellers about local ecosystems and cultural traditions.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 10: Ecotourism. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to practise responsible ecotourism in nature reserves before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and provide sustainable income for local villagers to conserve nature in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 10: Ecotourism)</i>"
