            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 1: A LONG AND HEALTHY LIFE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from maintaining a balanced diet, regular exercise and longevity. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen healthy habits. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for teenagers and parents to strengthen the immune system and prevent infectious diseases.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 1: A Long and Healthy Life. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to maintain a balanced diet and regular workout in daily life before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and increase life expectancy and boost daily mental energy in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 1: A Long and Healthy Life)</i>"
