            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 1: A LONG AND HEALTHY LIFE</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about maintaining a balanced diet, regular exercise and longevity. Rather than treating Unit 1: A Long and Healthy Life as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to strengthen the immune system and prevent infectious diseases.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to maintain a balanced diet and regular workout in daily life. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on healthy habits. Through these authentic tasks, teenagers and parents discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped increase life expectancy and boost daily mental energy. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making maintaining a balanced diet, regular exercise and longevity an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 1: A Long and Healthy Life)</i>"
