            "passage": "<b>YOUTH CLUB NOTICE: UNIT 2: THE GENERATION GAP</b>\nOur school English Club is launching a special thematic week dedicated to understanding generational differences and bridging the generation gap. Check out our highlights below: I think parents <b>(1)</b>______ listen to their children’s opinions before deciding which university they will attend. A <b>(2)</b>______ family consists of only two generations: parents and their children living under the same roof. In my family, my parents set strict rules: I <b>(3)</b>______ be home by 9:30 p.m. every evening.\nFrequent arguments over hairstyles, clothes and table manners are signs of the generation <b>(4)</b>______. Many young people refuse to follow in their parents’ <b>(5)</b>______ and want to start their own businesses. Teenagers ought <b>(6)</b>______ their grandparents’ life experience even when their views differ. Join our club this Friday to respect different generational viewpoints in extended and nuclear families together!\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success – Unit 2: The Generation Gap)</i>"
