            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 3: CITIES OF THE FUTURE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from smart cities, green skyscrapers and sustainable urban living. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen smart technologies. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for city dwellers and planners to use AI sensors to save energy and eliminate traffic jams.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 3: Cities of the Future. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to build sustainable and liveable smart cities in future urban centres before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and expand rooftop gardens and pedestrian zones for a greener environment in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 3: Cities of the Future)</i>"
