            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 4: ASEAN AND VIET NAM</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from ASEAN youth cooperation, cultural exchange and leadership. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen cultural exchange programmes. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for young delegates from ASEAN nations to promote solidarity, mutual understanding and peace among member states.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 4: ASEAN and Viet Nam. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to participate actively in ASEAN youth projects across the ASEAN region before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and develop leadership, communication and teamwork skills for youth in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 4: ASEAN and Viet Nam)</i>"
