            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 5: GLOBAL WARMING</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from cutting greenhouse gas emissions, soot and deforestation. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen climate actions. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for governments and citizens to cut down on carbon dioxide, methane and black carbon emissions.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 5: Global Warming. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to switch from fossil fuels to renewable energy around the world before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and slow down polar ice melting and protect coastal communities in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 5: Global Warming)</i>"
