            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 6: PRESERVING OUR HERITAGE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from preserving cultural and natural heritage sites across Viet Nam. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen heritage sites. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for young people and local artisans to pass down traditional folk arts like Quan Họ and Đờn Ca Tài Tử.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 6: Preserving Our Heritage. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to preserve and promote our national heritage across Viet Nam before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and protect ancient monuments and scenic landscapes from damage in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 6: Preserving Our Heritage)</i>"
