            "explanation": "Đoạn 1 trình bày các kết quả nghiên cứu làm nổi bật lợi ích của education options.",
            "passage": "<b>MAKING EDUCATION OPTIONS FOR SCHOOL-LEAVERS PART OF DAILY LIFE</b>\nTaking time to choose the right educational pathway after graduation may seem ordinary at first glance, yet a growing body of research highlights its transformative power. Studies show that well-designed education options help school-leavers and parents gain practical hands-on skills through apprenticeships. At the same time, these practices earn formal degrees or trade qualifications that match career goals and foster stronger cooperation at universities and vocational colleges.\nDespite these clear advantages, participation in education options has faced obstacles in recent years. Researchers report that <u><b>they</b></u> have been neglected in many busy communities due to modern time pressures. <u><b>Tight timetables, heavy workloads and a lack of practical guidance can all prevent people from maintaining positive routines.</b></u> Even when individuals want to improve, distractions often get in the way.\nThe encouraging news is that success does not require perfection from day one. Experts emphasise that building <u><b>practical</b></u> habits is about steady progress rather than instant results. School-leavers and parents can start with simple steps at universities and vocational colleges, share responsibilities and use practical checklists to stay on track. Those who understand the purpose behind choosing between university study and vocational training after high school become much more resilient and motivated.\nOf course, no single workshop or rule will solve every challenge overnight, and some groups need time to adapt. That is no reason to give up. Even one or two focused sessions a week can spark meaningful change, and the positive <u><b>qualification</b></u> will grow stronger over time. What matters most is the commitment people bring to supporting one another every day.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 7: Education Options for School-Leavers)</i>"
