            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 7: EDUCATION OPTIONS FOR SCHOOL-LEAVERS</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from choosing between university study and vocational training after high school. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen education options. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for school-leavers and parents to gain practical hands-on skills through apprenticeships.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 7: Education Options for School-Leavers. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to choose the right educational pathway after graduation at universities and vocational colleges before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and earn formal degrees or trade qualifications that match career goals in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 7: Education Options for School-Leavers)</i>"
