            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 7: EDUCATION OPTIONS FOR SCHOOL-LEAVERS</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about choosing between university study and vocational training after high school. Rather than treating Unit 7: Education Options for School-Leavers as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to gain practical hands-on skills through apprenticeships.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to choose the right educational pathway after graduation at universities and vocational colleges. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on education options. Through these authentic tasks, school-leavers and parents discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped earn formal degrees or trade qualifications that match career goals. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making choosing between university study and vocational training after high school an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 7: Education Options for School-Leavers)</i>"
