            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 9: SOCIAL ISSUES</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from addressing peer pressure, cyberbullying and body shaming among teens. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen social issues. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for students, counsellors and parents to protect teenagers from cyberbullying, body shaming and negative peer pressure.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 9: Social Issues. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to stand up against bullying and support victims in schools and online before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and create a safe, empathetic and supportive school environment for all in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 9: Social Issues)</i>"
