            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 10: THE ECOSYSTEM</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from conserving native flora and fauna, wetlands and food chains. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen natural ecosystems. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for biologists, rangers and students to protect native flora and fauna and keep food chains in balance.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 10: The Ecosystem. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to conserve biodiversity and restore degraded habitats in national parks and wetlands before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and prevent soil erosion, store carbon and shelter migratory birds in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 10: The Ecosystem)</i>"
