            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 1: LIFE STORIES WE ADMIRE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from admiring inspiring life stories, national heroes and innovators. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen inspiring biographies. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for young readers and historians to learn about the determination and selflessness of national heroes.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 1: Life Stories We Admire. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to admire and learn from great life stories in history and modern life before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and inspire teenagers to overcome obstacles and contribute to society in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 1: Life Stories We Admire)</i>"
