            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 2: A MULTICULTURAL WORLD</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from celebrating cultural diversity, traditional festivals and global cuisines. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen cultural traditions. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for students from diverse backgrounds to help people overcome culture shock and appreciate cultural diversity.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 2: A Multicultural World. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to respect and celebrate cultural diversity in a multicultural world before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and preserve national cultural identity in an age of globalisation in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 2: A Multicultural World)</i>"
