            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 4: URBANISATION</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from urbanisation trends, infrastructure challenges and sustainable city growth. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen urban developments. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for city planners and residents to upgrade public transport, schools and hospitals for growing populations.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 4: Urbanisation. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to plan urban expansion sustainably in rapidly growing cities before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and reduce traffic congestion, housing shortages and air pollution in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 4: Urbanisation)</i>"
