            "passage": "<b>MAKING THE WORLD OF WORK PART OF DAILY LIFE</b>\nTaking time to prepare a strong CV and develop workplace skills may seem ordinary at first glance, yet a growing body of research highlights its transformative power. Studies show that well-designed job opportunities help job applicants and employers gain valuable on-the-job training and communication skills. At the same time, these practices earn a fair wage while learning time management and responsibility and foster stronger cooperation in the modern workplace.\nDespite these clear advantages, participation in job opportunities has faced obstacles in recent years. Researchers report that <u><b>they</b></u> have been neglected in many busy communities due to modern time pressures. <u><b>Tight timetables, heavy workloads and a lack of practical guidance can all prevent people from maintaining positive routines.</b></u> Even when individuals want to improve, distractions often get in the way.\nThe encouraging news is that success does not require perfection from day one. Experts emphasise that building <u><b>rewarding</b></u> habits is about steady progress rather than instant results. Job applicants and employers can start with simple steps in the modern workplace, share responsibilities and use practical checklists to stay on track. Those who understand the purpose behind job requirements, working conditions and career preparation become much more resilient and motivated.\nOf course, no single workshop or rule will solve every challenge overnight, and some groups need time to adapt. That is no reason to give up. Even one or two focused sessions a week can spark meaningful change, and the positive <u><b>vacancy</b></u> will grow stronger over time. What matters most is the commitment people bring to supporting one another every day.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 5: The World of Work)</i>"
