            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 5: THE WORLD OF WORK</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from job requirements, working conditions and career preparation. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen job opportunities. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for job applicants and employers to gain valuable on-the-job training and communication skills.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 5: The World of Work. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to prepare a strong CV and develop workplace skills in the modern workplace before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and earn a fair wage while learning time management and responsibility in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 5: The World of Work)</i>"
