            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 6: ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from applications of artificial intelligence in education, healthcare and homes. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen AI applications. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for students, teachers and engineers to provide personalised learning feedback and automate routine tasks.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 6: Artificial Intelligence. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to use artificial intelligence responsibly and effectively in schools and smart homes before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and help doctors analyse medical scans and assist elderly people at home in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 6: Artificial Intelligence)</i>"
