            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 6: ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about applications of artificial intelligence in education, healthcare and homes. Rather than treating Unit 6: Artificial Intelligence as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to provide personalised learning feedback and automate routine tasks.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to use artificial intelligence responsibly and effectively in schools and smart homes. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on AI applications. Through these authentic tasks, students, teachers and engineers discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped help doctors analyse medical scans and assist elderly people at home. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making applications of artificial intelligence in education, healthcare and homes an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 6: Artificial Intelligence)</i>"
