            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 7: THE WORLD OF MASS MEDIA</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from digital media, fact-checking misinformation and responsible media use. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen mass media channels. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for journalists and netizens to deliver breaking news quickly and connect communities worldwide.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 7: The World of Mass Media. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to use mass media critically and responsibly across digital and print media before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and help citizens verify credible sources and stop the spread of fake news in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 7: The World of Mass Media)</i>"
