            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 7: THE WORLD OF MASS MEDIA</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about digital media, fact-checking misinformation and responsible media use. Rather than treating Unit 7: The World of Mass Media as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to deliver breaking news quickly and connect communities worldwide.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to use mass media critically and responsibly across digital and print media. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on mass media channels. Through these authentic tasks, journalists and netizens discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped help citizens verify credible sources and stop the spread of fake news. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making digital media, fact-checking misinformation and responsible media use an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 7: The World of Mass Media)</i>"
