            "passage": "<b>COMBINING TRADITIONAL VALUES WITH MODERN TOOLS IN UNIT 9: CAREER PATHS</b>\nIn the digital age, some commentators worry that modern technology might distract young people from exploring career paths, developing soft skills and adapting to automation. Yet recent educational projects show that when used wisely, digital tools can actually strengthen career paths. Shared mobile calendars, reminder apps and online group checklists make it easier than ever for school-leavers and career advisers to develop soft skills like critical thinking, teamwork and adaptability.\nOf course, technology alone cannot solve every problem. Researchers warn against relying passively on apps while ignoring face-to-face communication, as <u><b>they</b></u> are only tools in the hands of users. <u><b>Digital tools should serve as a practical bridge to support daily cooperation rather than a replacement for genuine human interaction.</b></u>\nWhen families and classmates combine smart reminders with warm personal encouragement, they can <u><b>preserve</b></u> the core spirit of Unit 9: Career Paths. For example, a quick evening message can remind everyone to build both technical expertise and soft skills in the changing job market before gathering for a friendly conversation.\nUltimately, blending modern convenience with timeless values helps communities <u><b>enhance</b></u> their daily routines and keep up with technological changes and choose a fulfilling career in a sustainable way.\n<i>(Adapted from Global Success Reading Series – Unit 9: Career Paths)</i>"
