            "passage": "<b>EXPERIENTIAL LEARNING AND THE FUTURE OF UNIT 9: CAREER PATHS</b>\nAcross Viet Nam, forward-thinking high schools are transforming how students learn about exploring career paths, developing soft skills and adapting to automation. Rather than treating Unit 9: Career Paths as a set of vocabulary items to memorise for a test, teachers are integrating experiential learning into every week of the semester. Educators agree that hands-on practice is <u><b>indispensable</b></u> if young people are to develop soft skills like critical thinking, teamwork and adaptability.\nIn these classrooms, students work in project teams to investigate real issues and propose ways to build both technical expertise and soft skills in the changing job market. For instance, learners might interview local residents, design bilingual awareness posters or organise a school-wide campaign on career paths. Through these authentic tasks, school-leavers and career advisers discover how their classroom English connects directly to everyday life.\nAssessment methods are evolving alongside teaching styles. <b>[I]</b> Instead of relying solely on written quizzes, schools evaluate how effectively students collaborate and apply their plans. <b>[II]</b> Each team keeps a reflective portfolio documenting the challenges they faced and how their actions helped keep up with technological changes and choose a fulfilling career. <b>[III]</b> This approach rewards creativity, persistence and genuine teamwork rather than rote memorisation. <b>[IV]</b>\nGraduates of experiential programmes consistently report higher confidence when entering university and the workplace. Students <u><b>who</b></u> have practised solving real-world problems in high school adapt much faster to new environments. By making exploring career paths, developing soft skills and adapting to automation an active, lived experience, education equips the next generation with both language proficiency and civic responsibility.\n<i>(Adapted from Modern Curriculum & Pedagogy Journal – Unit 9: Career Paths)</i>"
