            "text": "<b>Dear Kenji,</b>\na. Outside the classroom, we also take part in practical activities to maintain the habit of lifelong learning in community centres and online.\nb. How do students in Japan learn about this topic? Write back soon and tell me!\nc. This month in Viet Nam, high school students are studying Unit 10: Lifelong Learning, which focuses on lifelong learning, adult night classes and keeping the mind sharp.\nd. These experiences have taught my classmates and me how to broaden horizons, boost memory and keep the brain sharp in old age and help working adults update professional skills and adapt to new technology.\ne. Thank you for your postcard from Tokyo; I loved reading about your school festival.\n<b>Best wishes,</b>",
