            "tapescript": "PART 2 – (Questions 11–15) You will hear a conversation between Gemma and Bill about different sports. Mark the sentences as True (T) or False (F).\nGemma: Hi Bill! Have you decided which new sport we should sign up for at the community leisure centre this term?\nMr Bill: Well, Gemma, my older brother started a weightlifting class there last month. He says it’s brilliant for building strength, though he mentioned there are only two girls in a class of twenty-five people.\nGemma: Really? To be honest, weightlifting doesn’t appeal to me at all. I saw a documentary about weightlifting champions last night, and I definitely don’t want to end up looking all bulky and muscular like them!Besides, I’m stuck inside an office all week, so I much prefer doing outdoor activities in the fresh air.\nMr Bill: Fair enough. What about kayaking or windsurfing down at the lake, then? That’s outdoors!\nGemma: Oh, kayaking sounds fantastic! Let’s sign up for that!\nMr Bill: Erm... actually, Gemma, I’d rather not. I’ve never been keen on water sports. In fact, I hate getting into deep water.\nGemma: Do you? We’ve been friends for three years and I had no idea you disliked the water! Okay, scratch kayaking. What about hang-gliding off the ridge?\nMr Bill: Hang-gliding? Have you seen how high those cliffs are? No way—I’m terrified of heights, and the equipment hire costs a fortune anyway. Let’s try the weekend mountain-biking club in the forest instead.\nGemma: Mountain biking in the forest? Now that’s a great compromise. Let’s go for it!",
