            "passage": "<b>📋 PHIẾU GHI CHÉP BÀI NGHE — Temporary Patient Record Form</b><table class=\"w-full border-collapse border border-blue-300 mt-2 mb-1 text-sm bg-white\"><tr class=\"bg-blue-100 font-bold text-blue-900\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">1. Personal Details</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 w-1/3 font-semibold\">Name:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><i>Example:</i> <b>Peter Smith</b></td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Street address:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><b>(1)</b> _________________________</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Suburb:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><b>(2)</b> _________________________</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Phone number:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><b>(3)</b> _________________________</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-blue-100 font-bold text-blue-900\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">2. Details of Injury</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Sport:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">Tennis</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Type of injury:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><b>(4)</b> _________________________ knees</td></tr><tr><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2 font-semibold\">Date of injury:</td><td class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\"><b>(5)</b> _________________________</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-blue-100 font-bold text-blue-900\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">3. Previous Treatment and Current Problems</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">• The patient’s private doctor suggested treatment with <b>(6)</b> _________________________.<br>• The patient is unable to <b>(7)</b> _________________________ and he is experiencing some pain in his <b>(8)</b> _________________________ at night.</td></tr><tr class=\"bg-blue-100 font-bold text-blue-900\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">4. Advice Given</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"border border-blue-300 p-2\">• Stop using the <b>(9)</b> _________________________<br>• Do <b>(10)</b> _________________________ at home</td></tr></table>",
            "tapescript": "PART 1 – (Questions 1–10) You will hear a man talking first to a receptionist and then to a doctor at a health centre.\nReceptionist: Good morning, Sports Medicine Clinic. How can I help you?\nMr Peter Smith: Hello. I’m visiting from out of town and I’ve hurt my knees playing tennis. I’d like to see a doctor, please.\nReceptionist: Certainly. Since you’re a temporary patient, I’ll just take down a few details for our record form. What’s your full name?\nMr Peter Smith: It’s Peter Smith.\nReceptionist: And what’s your local street address while you’re staying here, Mr Smith?\nMr Peter Smith: I’m staying at my sister’s house at 73B High Street.\nReceptionist: 73B High Street. And which suburb is that in?\nMr Peter Smith: It’s in Northfield. N-O-R-T-H-F-I-E-L-D.\nReceptionist: Thank you. And a contact phone number in case we need to reach you?\nMr Peter Smith: You can reach me on 9487 3612.\nReceptionist: Lovely. Take a seat and Dr Clara will see you right away.\nMrs Clara: Come in, Mr Smith. I see from the note that you injured yourself playing tennis. What seems to be the trouble?\nMr Peter Smith: Yes, Doctor. Both of my knees are badly sprained. I lunged for a backhand shot and twisted them awkwardly.\nMrs Clara: I see—sprained knees can be very painful. When exactly did this happen?\nMr Peter Smith: It happened on the eighteenth of June—just over a week ago.\nMrs Clara: Have you seen anyone about it since the eighteenth of June?\nMr Peter Smith: Yes, my private doctor back home examined me the next day and suggested treatment with ice packs twice a day.\nMrs Clara: Did the ice packs help?\nMr Peter Smith: They reduced the swelling a little, but right now I’m still unable to walk upstairs without sharp pain, and strangely enough, I’m also experiencing some pain in my lower back at night when I lie down.\nMrs Clara: That’s because you’re walking stiffly to protect your knees, which strains your lower back. Have you been using any gym equipment this week?\nMr Peter Smith: Well, I’ve been using an exercise bike in my sister’s garage to try to keep fit.\nMrs Clara: Right, first of all, you must stop using the exercise bike immediately—it’s putting far too much pressure on the knee joints. Instead, I’m going to show you how to do gentle stretching exercises at home twice a day until the ligaments heal.",
